  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AACC - Strengthening Religious Actors structures for a peaceful and just Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to strengthen the role of religious actors in peacebuilding, governance, gender justice, and economic advocacy across Africa. The project focuses on empowering faith leaders, women, and youth to engage in conflict resolution, governance accountability, gender-based violence (GBV) prevention, and economic justice advocacy to promote sustainable peace and development. 

Key intervention areas are Peacebuilding and Conflict resolution (including trauma healing, faith-based mediation and dialogue; Gender Justice and GBV Prevention (incl. challenging gender norms and leadership programmes for women in peacebuilding; Economic Justice and Debt Advocacy (Incl, engaging faith leaders and youth in debt advocacy); Youth Civic Engagement and Digital Advocacy (incl. campaigns against extremism); and Climate and Environmental Justice (incl. Equipping faith leaders to advocate for climate justice and sustainable resource management).</narrative>
  </description>
